            <div xml:id="d986">

                <pb facs="1130" n="1018" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1018"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9417/64</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of Commerce</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Roper</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-04">November 4, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am sending you herewith a
                    copy of the letter of October 28, addressed to the President, with reference to
                    competing Japanese textiles, and signed by the four members of the Cabinet
                    Textile Committee.</p>
                <p>The President returned the letter to me with the notation: “I approve—go ahead.”
                    This constitutes authority for the State Department to proceed immediately with
                    its negotiations with the Japanese government to fulfill the purposes as
                    recommended to the President.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniel C. Roper</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
